The \intertext command is defined in the amsmath package, so you need to load that package first. Also, you should use \frac rather than \dfrac for this purpose.

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}

\begin{document}

\begin{align*}
\frac{\partial}{\partial t} \intertext{and} \frac{\partial^2}{\partial t^2}
\end{align*}

\end{document}
